# 2026-07-30 implementation notes
- Comments are lexer trivia (the lexer already recorded their spans for
  the 8-2 refusal) carried by a CommentSink threaded through the AST
  printer: standalone comments flush before the next stmt/decl at its
  indent (keeping one blank line if the source had one); trailing
  comments re-attach to their statement's formatted line; shebangs stay
  first. The 8-2 refusal is removed; docs/fmt.md documents the rules.
- The corpus round-trip property (every snippets/ file: fmt twice is
  idempotent, comment multiset preserved) exposed a PILE of latent
  printer bugs — the AST printer had never round-tripped real programs:
  params printed without parens/`as`/commas, lambdas printed as the
  invalid `(x) => ...` placeholder, struct literals used braces, type
  fields used `is`, enum variants and ctor patterns used `of`, match
  arms used `=>`, calls/methods dropped parentheses, if-expressions
  printed `if..then..else`, fn types printed `->`, `err` decls/raises
  printed `error`/`throw`, pipes printed `|>` (the operator is `~` —
  `|>` lexes as `|` + ident `gt`!), and yield/spawn/channel/OfCall/
  NamedArg all printed `...`. All fixed; formatted output now reparses
  to the same program for the entire corpus.
- String quoting on reprint preserves MEANING: raw strings containing
  braces (and no double quote) reprint double-quoted; a string with
  braces AND double quotes stays single-quoted (invalid interpolations
  are literal, so the reparse is identical — there are no escape
  sequences in the lexer).
- Found but not fixed here: snippets/guide_tour.jn's pipeline section
  uses `|>`, which parses as bitwise-or plus a bare `gt` identifier —
  the section is semantically broken source (the formatter now prints
  what it actually parses as). Candidate cleanup for 8-26's docs pass.
